cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this build method, cite it as below and state which preset you used."
title: "Anthropic Serif CJK Rebuild"
abstract: "A reproducible rebuild of a multilingual serif font. As of 2026-11-24 the repository ships exactly one font binary, fonts/SerifCJKExtension-Standard.ttf (the cjk production build); all other outputs remain local-only. The reader can also supply a legally obtained proprietary Latin base plus two SIL OFL sources and run scripts/build_cjk.py locally. An optional L3 stroke-skeleton post-processing pipeline is also provided. Four presets produce cjk (31,724 glyphs), cjk-bold (same coverage, heavier Chinese), multilingual (33,897 glyphs, adds Latin Extended, Greek and Cyrillic) and full (47,092 glyphs / 46,963 code points, adds kana, Hangul and CJK symbols). The output is renamed to Serif CJK Extension by default and preserves all upstream Latin outlines, 19 GSUB features and 2 GPOS features. Repository material is MIT; generated added outlines are SIL OFL 1.1; the upstream Latin outlines inside the shipped TTF are proprietary and their public redistribution status is unresolved. See LICENSE and docs/COMPLIANCE.md."
